 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "taanit.19a.15",
   "daf": "19a",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "וְכֵן שֶׁפָּסְקוּ גְּשָׁמִים בֵּין גֶּשֶׁם לְגֶשֶׁם כּוּ׳. מַאי מַכַּת בַּצּוֹרֶת? אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר רַב: מַכָּה הַמְּבִיאָה לִידֵי בַּצּוֹרֶת. אָמַר רַב נַחְמָן: נַהֲרָא אַנַּהֲרָא —",
   "en": "The mishna further taught: «And likewise,» if «rain ceased» for a period of «forty days» between «one rainfall and another,» they cry out about this, because it is a plague of drought. The Gemara asks: «What is» the meaning of the phrase: «A plague of drought?» Isn’t this simply a drought? «Rav Yehuda said» that «Rav said:» The mishna means that a period of forty days between one rainfall and the next «is a plague that» may «cause a drought.» In this regard, «Rav Naḥman said:» When crops do not grow in one place due to lack of rain and must be imported by means of one «river to» another «river,»"
  }
 ],
